<#ch-choose-2>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-choose> ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Shall we, or would you like to?

**-(으)ㄹ까요?** puts an idea up for the other person to decide: "shall we?" or "shall I?". Add -ㄹ까요 to a stem that ends in a vowel or ㄹ, and -을까요 after any other consonant: 가다 becomes 갈까요?, 만들다 becomes 만들까요?, 먹다 becomes 먹을까요?

**-(으)ㄹ래요?** asks what the other person wants: "do you want to?", "would you like to?". It is a warm invitation between peers. It is built the same way: 갈래요?, 만들래요?, 먹을래요? In an answer it says what you want: 저는 국수 먹을래요 (I'd like noodles).

**-(으)러 가다** means going somewhere to do something. Add -러 after a vowel or ㄹ and -으러 after another consonant: 먹으러 가요 (go to eat), 커피 마시러 가요 (go for a coffee).

**민지:** 비빔밥 먹으러 갈래요?\\
*Do you want to go and have bibimbap?*

**알렉스:** 좋아요. 지금 갈까요?\\
*Sure. Shall we go now?*

---

**안 and 못.** Both make a verb negative and stand right before it. 안 says you don't, by choice or habit. 못 says you can't: something stops you.

- **저는 고기를 안 먹어요**: "I don't eat meat." This is what a vegetarian says: a choice.
- **매운 건 잘 못 먹어요**: "I'm not good with spicy food." Literally "I can't eat spicy things well". This is the honest answer to 매운 거 잘 먹어요?

Say 고기를 못 먹어요 and you can't eat meat, perhaps for your health; say 매운 건 안 먹어요 and you choose not to.

**매운 건** is short for 매운 것은: 은 sets spicy food apart from the rest, as in "spicy food, I'm not good with". In the question it is 매운 거, short for 매운 것.

**잘 못** with a space means "not well". Written together, 잘못 means a mistake or wrongly: 잘못 먹었어요 is "I ate something that disagreed with me"."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-choose-2a> ,
                         <#q-choose-2b> ,
                         <#q-choose-2c> .

<#q-choose-2a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "비빔밥 먹으러 갈래요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Do you want to go and have bibimbap?"@en ,
                    "Vill du gå och äta bibimbap?"@sv ,
                    "Hast du Lust, Bibimbap essen zu gehen?"@de ,
                    "¿Quieres ir a comer bibimbap?"@es ,
                    "Tu veux aller manger un bibimbap ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "An invitation to a friend or acquaintance, in polite 해요체. -(으)러 가다 means going somewhere to do something, and -(으)ㄹ래요? asks what the other person would like. Answer 좋아요, 같이 가요! or, to say no gently, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@en ,
                        "En inbjudan till en vän eller bekant, i artig 해요체. -(으)러 가다 betyder att gå någonstans för att göra något, och -(으)ㄹ래요? frågar vad den andra vill. Svara 좋아요, 같이 가요! eller, för att säga nej vänligt, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@sv ,
                        "Eine Einladung an Freunde oder Bekannte, im höflichen 해요체. -(으)러 가다 heißt, irgendwohin gehen, um etwas zu tun, und -(으)ㄹ래요? fragt, was der andere möchte. Antwort: 좋아요, 같이 가요! oder, als sanftes Nein, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@de ,
                        "Una invitación a un amigo o conocido, en el estilo cortés 해요체. -(으)러 가다 es ir a algún sitio a hacer algo, y -(으)ㄹ래요? pregunta qué quiere el otro. Se responde 좋아요, 같이 가요! o, para decir que no con suavidad, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@es ,
                        "Une invitation à un ami ou une connaissance, au style poli 해요체. -(으)러 가다 veut dire aller quelque part pour faire quelque chose, et -(으)ㄹ래요? demande ce que l'autre veut. On répond 좋아요, 같이 가요! ou, pour refuser gentiment, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-choose-2a-d1> ,
                          <#q-choose-2a-d2> ,
                          <#q-choose-2a-d3> .

<#q-choose-2a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Have you ever had bibimbap?"@en ,
                              "Har du ätit bibimbap förut?"@sv ,
                              "Hast du schon mal Bibimbap gegessen?"@de ,
                              "¿Has comido bibimbap alguna vez?"@es ,
                              "Tu as déjà mangé un bibimbap ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요?; -(으)ㄹ래요? invites, it does not ask about the past."@en ,
                              "Det vore 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요?; -(으)ㄹ래요? bjuder in, den frågar inte om det som har hänt."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요?; -(으)ㄹ래요? lädt ein und fragt nicht nach der Vergangenheit."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요?; -(으)ㄹ래요? invita, no pregunta por el pasado."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요? ; -(으)ㄹ래요? invite, il ne porte pas sur le passé."@fr .

<#q-choose-2a-d2>
