<#ch-choose-3>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-choose> ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Anything is fine

*Another evening, another way it goes: this time Minji wants Alex to choose.*

**민지:** 오늘은 알렉스 씨가 골라요. 뭐 먹을래요?\\
*You choose today, Alex. What would you like?*

**알렉스:** 저는 아무거나 잘 먹어요. 민지 씨가 정해요.\\
*I'm happy to eat anything. You decide, Minji.*

**민지:** 그럼 삼겹살 어때요?\\
*How about grilled pork belly, then?*

**알렉스:** 음, 고기는 좀 그래요. 어제 먹었어요.\\
*Hmm, I'd rather not have meat. I had it yesterday.*

**민지:** 하하, 알겠어요. 그럼 국수 어때요?\\
*Ha, all right. How about noodles, then?*

**알렉스:** 좋아요! 국수 먹으러 가요.\\
*Great! Let's go and have noodles.*

---

**저는 아무거나 잘 먹어요**: "I'm happy to eat anything", literally "I eat anything well". It sounds easygoing, but it hands the decision back. Koreans joke about the friend who says 아무거나 and then turns ideas down, as Alex just did with 삼겹살. If you really don't mind, add a suggestion or say who should decide, like 민지 씨가 정해요 (you decide, Minji).

**고기는 좀 그래요**: "I'd rather not have meat." 좀 그래요, roughly "it's a bit so-so", turns an idea down without a flat 싫어요 (I don't want to), which sounds blunt between people who are still polite with each other. A reason after it, like 어제 먹었어요 (I had it yesterday), makes it softer still.

**Eating together:** a Korean meal is usually shared, with side dishes and often a stew in the middle of the table. So choosing is a joint decision, and 같이 (together) comes up all the time."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-choose-3a> ,
                         <#q-choose-3b> .

<#q-choose-3a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "저는 아무거나 잘 먹어요"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "I'm happy to eat anything"@en ,
                    "Jag äter vad som helst"@sv ,
                    "Ich esse alles"@de ,
                    "Yo como de todo"@es ,
                    "Je mange de tout"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said when someone asks what you would like to eat, in polite 해요체. Literally \"I eat anything well\". It hands the choice back, so a suggestion or 정해 주세요 (please decide) often follows."@en ,
                        "Sägs när någon frågar vad man vill äta, i artig 해요체. Ordagrant ”jag äter vad som helst bra”. Det lämnar tillbaka valet, så ofta följer ett förslag eller 정해 주세요 (bestäm du)."@sv ,
                        "Sagt man, wenn jemand fragt, was man essen möchte, im höflichen 해요체. Wörtlich „ich esse alles gut“. Damit gibt man die Wahl zurück, deshalb folgt oft ein Vorschlag oder 정해 주세요 (entscheide du)."@de ,
                        "Se dice cuando alguien pregunta qué quieres comer, en el estilo cortés 해요체. Literalmente «como bien cualquier cosa». Devuelve la decisión, así que a menudo sigue una propuesta o 정해 주세요 (decide tú)."@es ,
                        "Se dit quand quelqu'un demande ce qu'on veut manger, au style poli 해요체. Littéralement « je mange bien n'importe quoi ». Cela renvoie le choix à l'autre, aussi suit souvent une proposition ou 정해 주세요 (décide, toi)."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-choose-3a-d1> ,
                          <#q-choose-3a-d2> ,
                          <#q-choose-3a-d3> .

<#q-choose-3a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "I'm not very hungry"@en ,
                              "Jag är inte så hungrig"@sv ,
                              "Ich habe nicht so viel Hunger"@de ,
                              "No tengo mucha hambre"@es ,
                              "Je n'ai pas très faim"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 배가 별로 안 고파요; 아무거나 잘 먹어요 says any food is fine."@en ,
                              "Det vore 배가 별로 안 고파요; 아무거나 잘 먹어요 säger att all mat går bra."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 배가 별로 안 고파요; 아무거나 잘 먹어요 sagt, dass jedes Essen recht ist."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 배가 별로 안 고파요; 아무거나 잘 먹어요 dice que cualquier comida vale."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 배가 별로 안 고파요 ; 아무거나 잘 먹어요 dit que tout plat convient."@fr .

