# Chapter 2: A small 찌개 restaurant.
<#ch-restaurant>
    a solid-memo:Chapter ,
      schema:Syllabus ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <> ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    dcterms:title "A small 찌개 restaurant"@en ,
                  "En liten 찌개-restaurang"@sv ,
                  "Ein kleines 찌개-Restaurant"@de ,
                  "Un pequeño restaurante de 찌개"@es ,
                  "Un petit restaurant de 찌개"@fr ,
                  "찌개집에서"@ko ;
    dcterms:description "Alex and Minji have dinner at a small stew restaurant: getting a table, ordering by the portion, asking for more rice and side dishes, and finding out how to eat a pot that cooks at the table. Ends with a review of the chapter."@en ,
                        "Alex och Minji äter middag på en liten grytrestaurang: de får ett bord, beställer per portion, ber om mer ris och fler sidorätter och tar reda på hur man äter en gryta som kokar på bordet. Avslutas med en repetition av kapitlet."@sv ,
                        "Alex und Minji essen in einem kleinen Eintopfrestaurant zu Abend: einen Tisch bekommen, portionsweise bestellen, um mehr Reis und Beilagen bitten und herausfinden, wie man einen Topf isst, der am Tisch gart. Endet mit einer Wiederholung des Kapitels."@de ,
                        "Alex y Minji cenan en un pequeño restaurante de estofados: conseguir mesa, pedir por raciones, pedir más arroz y acompañamientos y descubrir cómo se come una olla que se cocina en la mesa. Termina con un repaso del capítulo."@es ,
                        "Alex et Minji dînent dans un petit restaurant de ragoûts : trouver une table, commander à la portion, demander plus de riz et d'accompagnements, et découvrir comment manger une marmite qui cuit à table. Se termine par une révision du chapitre."@fr ;
    solid-memo:reviewQuestion <#q-restaurant-r01> ,
                              <#q-restaurant-r02> .

<#ch-restaurant-1>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-restaurant> ;
    schema:position 0 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## A table for two

*Twenty minutes later. The small 찌개 restaurant Minji knows is in a side street near Hongik University station, and it is already filling up.*

**사장님:** 어서 오세요. 몇 분이세요?\\
*Welcome. How many of you are there?*

**민지:** 두 명이에요.\\
*Two.*

**사장님:** 편한 자리에 앉으세요.\\
*Sit wherever you like.*

**민지:** 여기는 김치찌개가 진짜 맛있어요.\\
*The kimchi stew here is really good.*

**알렉스:** 그럼 그걸로 해요. 사장님, 김치찌개 2인분 주세요.\\
*Let's have that, then. Excuse me, kimchi stew for two, please.*

**사장님:** 네. 물은 셀프예요.\\
*Sure. Water is self-service.*

**민지:** 제가 가져올게요.\\
*I'll get it.*

---

**몇 분이세요?**: "How many of you are there?" 분 is the honorific counter for people, used by staff to honor the customer. You answer with the plain counter 명: 두 명이에요, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases.

**편한 자리에 앉으세요**: "Sit wherever you like." Literally "sit in a comfortable seat": the table is your choice. 앉으세요 is 앉다 with -시-.

**물은 셀프예요**: "Water is self-service." 셀프 comes from English and means you fetch it yourself, from a water dispenser or a fridge by the wall, with the cups next to it.

**사장님** means owner or boss. In a small restaurant it is the usual way to call the person serving you. Nobody shows you to a table there: you sit down, and the order is taken at the table."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-restaurant-1a> ,
                         <#q-restaurant-1b> .

<#q-restaurant-1a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "편한 자리에 앉으세요"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Sit wherever you like"@en ,
                    "Sätt er var ni vill"@sv ,
                    "Setzen Sie sich, wo Sie möchten"@de ,
                    "Siéntense donde quieran"@es ,
                    "Installez-vous où vous voulez"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said by restaurant staff to customers who may pick any free table, in polite 해요체 with -시- honoring the customer. Literally \"sit in a comfortable seat\". You answer 네 and choose a table."@en ,
                        "Sägs av restaurangpersonal till gäster som får välja vilket ledigt bord som helst, i artig 해요체 med -시- som hedrar gästen. Ordagrant ”sitt på en bekväm plats”. Du svarar 네 och väljer ett bord."@sv ,
                        "Sagt das Restaurantpersonal zu Gästen, die sich einen freien Tisch aussuchen dürfen, im höflichen 해요체 mit -시-, das den Gast ehrt. Wörtlich „setzen Sie sich auf einen bequemen Platz“. Man antwortet 네 und sucht sich einen Tisch aus."@de ,
                        "Lo dice el personal de un restaurante a clientes que pueden elegir cualquier mesa libre, en el estilo cortés 해요체 con -시-, que honra al cliente. Literalmente «siéntese en un sitio cómodo». Se responde 네 y se elige una mesa."@es ,
                        "Dit par le personnel d'un restaurant à des clients qui peuvent choisir n'importe quelle table libre, au style poli 해요체 avec -시-, qui honore le client. Littéralement « asseyez-vous à une place confortable ». On répond 네 et on choisit une table."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-restaurant-1a-d1> ,
                          <#q-restaurant-1a-d2> ,
                          <#q-restaurant-1a-d3> .

<#q-restaurant-1a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Wait here a moment"@en ,
                              "Vänta här en stund"@sv ,
                              "Warten Sie hier einen Moment"@de ,
                              "Esperen aquí un momento"@es ,
                              "Attendez ici un instant"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 여기서 잠깐 기다려 주세요; 앉으세요 asks you to sit down."@en ,
                              "Det vore 여기서 잠깐 기다려 주세요; 앉으세요 ber er sätta er."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 여기서 잠깐 기다려 주세요; 앉으세요 bittet Sie, sich zu setzen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 여기서 잠깐 기다려 주세요; 앉으세요 les pide que se sienten."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 여기서 잠깐 기다려 주세요 ; 앉으세요 vous demande de vous asseoir."@fr .

<#q-restaurant-1a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Sit by the window"@en ,
                              "Sätt er vid fönstret"@sv ,
                              "Setzen Sie sich ans Fenster"@de ,
                              "Siéntense junto a la ventana"@es ,
                              "Installez-vous près de la fenêtre"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 창가 자리에 앉으세요; 편한 means comfortable, so the seat is your choice."@en ,
                              "Det vore 창가 자리에 앉으세요; 편한 betyder bekväm, så ni väljer platsen själva."@sv ,
