<#ch-restaurant-3>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-restaurant> ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## A pot that cooks at the table

*Some 찌개 places bring the pot raw and set it on a gas burner on your table. This is how the same evening could go at a 부대찌개 place.*

**사장님:** 부대찌개 2인분 나왔습니다. 다 끓으면 드세요.\\
*Here's your army stew for two. Start eating once it's boiling.*

**알렉스:** 이거 어떻게 먹어요?\\
*How do you eat this?*

**민지:** 끓으면 국자로 덜어서 먹어요.\\
*Once it boils, you serve yourself with the ladle.*

**알렉스:** 사장님, 앞접시 좀 주세요.\\
*Excuse me, could we have some small plates?*

**사장님:** 네, 여기 있어요.\\
*Sure, here you are.*

---

**이거 어떻게 먹어요?**: "How do you eat this?" Ask it about any dish you don't know; the answer often starts with 이렇게 (like this).

**앞접시 좀 주세요**: "Some small plates, please." 앞접시 is the small plate in front of you (앞, front, and 접시, plate), for food from the shared pot.

**다 끓으면 드세요**: "Start eating once it's boiling." 다 means fully, 끓다 is to boil, -(으)면 means once or when, and 드세요 is 드시다, the honorific of 먹다, in 해요체.

**Culture note:** A 찌개 is shared: everyone eats from the same pot. 반찬 are free and refilled when you ask, while 공깃밥 may cost extra. Spoons and chopsticks are often in a drawer built into the side of the table or in a box on it. You call the staff with 저기요, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases, or with 사장님, and you usually pay at the counter on the way out."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-restaurant-3a> ,
                         <#q-restaurant-3b> .

<#q-restaurant-3a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "이거 어떻게 먹어요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "How do you eat this?"@en ,
                    "Hur äter man det här?"@sv ,
                    "Wie isst man das?"@de ,
                    "¿Cómo se come esto?"@es ,
                    "Comment ça se mange ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Asked about an unfamiliar dish, to a friend or the staff, in polite 해요체. The answer often starts with 이렇게 (like this), and staff may say 끓으면 드세요."@en ,
                        "Frågas om en okänd rätt, till en vän eller personalen, i artig 해요체. Svaret börjar ofta med 이렇게 (så här), och personalen kan säga 끓으면 드세요."@sv ,
                        "Gefragt bei einem unbekannten Gericht, an einen Freund oder das Personal, im höflichen 해요체. Die Antwort beginnt oft mit 이렇게 (so), und das Personal sagt vielleicht 끓으면 드세요."@de ,
                        "Se pregunta ante un plato desconocido, a un amigo o al personal, en el estilo cortés 해요체. La respuesta suele empezar por 이렇게 (así), y el personal puede decir 끓으면 드세요."@es ,
                        "Se demande devant un plat inconnu, à un ami ou au personnel, au style poli 해요체. La réponse commence souvent par 이렇게 (comme ça), et le personnel peut dire 끓으면 드세요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-restaurant-3a-d1> ,
                          <#q-restaurant-3a-d2> ,
                          <#q-restaurant-3a-d3> .

