<#q-restaurant-r02-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Don't eat it yet"@en ,
                              "Ät inte än"@sv ,
                              "Essen Sie noch nicht"@de ,
                              "No coman todavía"@es ,
                              "Ne mangez pas encore"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 아직 드시지 마세요; 다 끓으면 드세요 tells you when to start."@en ,
                              "Det vore 아직 드시지 마세요; 다 끓으면 드세요 säger när du kan börja."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 아직 드시지 마세요; 다 끓으면 드세요 sagt, wann man anfangen kann."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 아직 드시지 마세요; 다 끓으면 드세요 dice cuándo se puede empezar."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 아직 드시지 마세요 ; 다 끓으면 드세요 dit quand on peut commencer."@fr .

# Chapter 3: Who pays?
<#ch-paying>
    a solid-memo:Chapter ,
      schema:Syllabus ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <> ;
    schema:position 3 ;
    dcterms:title "Who pays?"@en ,
                  "Vem betalar?"@sv ,
                  "Wer zahlt?"@de ,
                  "¿Quién paga?"@es ,
                  "Qui paie ?"@fr ,
                  "누가 낼까요?"@ko ;
    dcterms:description "Dinner is over, and Alex and Minji are at the counter: treating someone and accepting a treat, offering to pay next time or for the coffee, and splitting the bill. Ends with a review of the chapter."@en ,
                        "Middagen är slut, och Alex och Minji står vid kassan: bjuda någon och ta emot en bjudning, erbjuda sig att betala nästa gång eller för kaffet, och dela på notan. Avslutas med en repetition av kapitlet."@sv ,
                        "Das Essen ist vorbei, und Alex und Minji stehen an der Kasse: jemanden einladen und eine Einladung annehmen, anbieten, das nächste Mal zu zahlen oder den Kaffee zu übernehmen, und die Rechnung teilen. Endet mit einer Wiederholung des Kapitels."@de ,
                        "La cena ha terminado y Alex y Minji están en la caja: invitar a alguien y aceptar una invitación, ofrecerse a pagar la próxima vez o el café, y pagar a medias. Termina con un repaso del capítulo."@es ,
                        "Le dîner est fini, et Alex et Minji sont à la caisse : inviter quelqu'un et accepter une invitation, proposer de payer la prochaine fois ou le café, et partager l'addition. Se termine par une révision du chapitre."@fr ;
    solid-memo:reviewQuestion <#q-paying-r01> ,
                              <#q-paying-r02> .

<#ch-paying-1>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-paying> ;
    schema:position 0 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## The bill

*Seven o'clock, the same Saturday evening. The kimchi stew is finished, and Alex gets up and goes to the counter by the door.*

**알렉스:** 사장님, 계산할게요.\\
*Excuse me, I'd like to pay.*

**사장님:** 네. 김치찌개 2인분, 공깃밥 하나, 사이다 한 병이요. 이만 삼천 원입니다.\\
*Sure. Kimchi stew for two, one rice and a bottle of lemon-lime soda. That's 23,000 won.*

**민지:** 잠깐만요! 오늘은 제가 살게요.\\
*Hang on! It's my treat today.*

**알렉스:** 아니에요, 같이 내요.\\
*Oh no, let's pay together.*

**민지:** 괜찮아요. 알렉스 씨 서울에 온 거 환영하는 의미로요.\\
*It's fine. Think of it as a welcome to Seoul.*

**알렉스:** 그럼 잘 먹었어요, 고마워요. 다음에는 제가 살게요.\\
*Then thank you for dinner. Next time it's on me.*

**민지:** 좋아요!\\
*Deal!*

**사장님:** 카드 여기 꽂아 주세요. … 영수증 드릴까요?\\
*Please put your card in here. … Would you like the receipt?*

**민지:** 아니요, 괜찮아요.\\
*No, thank you.*

---

**오늘은 제가 살게요**: "It's my treat today." 사다 means to buy, and also to buy something for someone, to treat them: 밥을 사다 is to buy someone a meal. 은 in 오늘은 sets today apart from other days: today, it's me.

**아니에요, 같이 내요**: "Oh no, let's pay together." Turning a treat down once, politely, is usual before accepting it; keep refusing and it turns into a tug of war at the register. 내다 means to pay.

**다음에는 제가 살게요**: "Next time it's on me." This is how a treat is accepted: thanks with 잘 먹었어요, 고마워요, then a promise to return it. 잘 먹었어요 is the 해요체 of 잘 먹었습니다, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases.

**At the counter:** 계산하다 is to pay the bill, so 계산할게요 tells the owner you are ready to pay; the next step explains -(으)ㄹ게요. 이만 삼천 원입니다 is 합쇼체, the formal style staff often use for a total. 꽂아 주세요 asks you to put the card into the slot of the card reader (꽂다, to insert). **영수증 드릴까요?** is "Would you like the receipt?", with the humble 드리다 the café staff used; 아니요, 괜찮아요 you know from Everyday Korean phrases."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-paying-1a> ,
                         <#q-paying-1b> .

<#q-paying-1a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-28T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "오늘은 제가 살게요"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "It's my treat today"@en ,
                    "I dag bjuder jag"@sv ,
                    "Heute lade ich dich ein"@de ,
                    "Hoy invito yo"@es ,
                    "Aujourd'hui, c'est moi qui invite"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said to a friend or acquaintance before a meal or at the end of one, often at the counter, in polite 해요체, offering to pay for both. 사다 means to buy, and also to treat someone; 오늘은 sets today apart from other days. The other person often protests once, then accepts with 잘 먹었어요, 고마워요 or, before the meal, 잘 먹을게요."@en ,
                        "Sägs till en vän eller bekant före en måltid eller i slutet av den, ofta vid kassan, i artig 해요체, när man erbjuder sig att betala för båda. 사다 betyder köpa, och även bjuda någon; 오늘은 ställer i dag mot andra dagar. Den andra protesterar ofta en gång och tackar sedan ja med 잘 먹었어요, 고마워요 eller, före måltiden, 잘 먹을게요."@sv ,
                        "Sagt man vor dem Essen oder am Ende, oft an der Kasse, zu Freunden oder Bekannten, im höflichen 해요체, wenn man für beide zahlen möchte. 사다 heißt kaufen und auch jemanden einladen; 오늘은 stellt heute anderen Tagen gegenüber. Der andere wehrt oft einmal ab und nimmt dann mit 잘 먹었어요, 고마워요 an oder, vor dem Essen, mit 잘 먹을게요."@de ,
                        "Se dice a un amigo o conocido antes de una comida o al final, a menudo en la caja, en el estilo cortés 해요체, al ofrecerse a pagar por los dos. 사다 significa comprar y también invitar a alguien; 오늘은 contrapone hoy a otros días. El otro suele protestar una vez y luego acepta con 잘 먹었어요, 고마워요 o, antes de comer, con 잘 먹을게요."@es ,
                        "Se dit à un ami ou une connaissance avant un repas ou à la fin, souvent à la caisse, au style poli 해요체, pour proposer de payer pour les deux. 사다 veut dire acheter, et aussi inviter quelqu'un ; 오늘은 oppose aujourd'hui aux autres jours. L'autre proteste souvent une fois, puis accepte avec 잘 먹었어요, 고마워요 ou, avant le repas, avec 잘 먹을게요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-paying-1a-d1> ,
                          <#q-paying-1a-d2> ,
                          <#q-paying-1a-d3> .

<#q-paying-1a-d1>
