<#q-paying-1b-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Next time I'll do the shopping"@en ,
                              "Nästa gång handlar jag"@sv ,
                              "Nächstes Mal kaufe ich ein"@de ,
                              "La próxima vez hago yo la compra"@es ,
                              "La prochaine fois, c'est moi qui fais les courses"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 다음에는 제가 장 볼게요; after a meal, 사다 with no object means paying for the other person."@en ,
                              "Det vore 다음에는 제가 장 볼게요; efter en måltid betyder 사다 utan objekt att betala för den andra."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 다음에는 제가 장 볼게요; nach einem Essen heißt 사다 ohne Objekt, für den anderen zu bezahlen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 다음에는 제가 장 볼게요; después de una comida, 사다 sin complemento significa pagar por el otro."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 다음에는 제가 장 볼게요 ; après un repas, 사다 sans complément veut dire payer pour l'autre."@fr .

<#ch-paying-2>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-paying> ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## I'll do it: -(으)ㄹ게요

*Outside the restaurant, Alex has an idea.*

**알렉스:** 그럼 커피는 제가 살게요. 근처에 카페 있어요?\\
*Then the coffee's on me. Is there a café nearby?*

**민지:** 좋아요, 잘 마실게요! 저기 모퉁이에 하나 있어요.\\
*Great, thanks, I'll enjoy it! There's one on the corner over there.*

**-(으)ㄹ게요** says what you will do, decided with the other person in mind: an offer, a promise, or "I'll do that, then". Add -ㄹ게요 to a stem that ends in a vowel or ㄹ, and -을게요 after any other consonant:

- 사다 → 살게요 (it's on me)
- 내다 → 낼게요 (I'll pay)
- 계산하다 → 계산할게요 (I'll settle the bill)
- 마시다 → 마실게요 (I'll drink it)
- 만들다 → 만들게요 (I'll make it)
- 먹다 → 먹을게요 (I'll eat it)

It is said as if written 께요: 살게요 sounds like 살께요. It is only about what the speaker will do, so it goes with 제가 or 저는, and it is never a question. To offer with a question, use -(으)ㄹ까요?, met when choosing dinner: 제가 살까요? (shall I pay?). The plain present 제가 사요 can make the same offer, but plainly; 제가 살게요 adds that you are deciding it for the listener's sake.

**잘 마실게요**: "Thanks, I'll enjoy the drink." You say it to the person treating you, before you drink, as you say 잘 먹을게요 before a meal someone buys you. Both are friendly cousins of 잘 먹겠습니다, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases.

---

**은/는 for contrast.** 커피는 제가 살게요 sets the coffee against the meal: the meal was you, the coffee is me. Spelled out, it would be 밥은 민지 씨가 샀으니까 커피는 제가 살게요. 오늘은 and 다음에는 in the scene work the same way: today, or next time, as opposed to other times. 은 follows a consonant, 는 a vowel.

**사다, 내다 or 계산하다?** All three come up when paying.

- **사다**, to buy, also means to buy for someone, to treat: 제가 살게요 always means the speaker pays for the other person too.
- **내다**, to pay out, is about the money: the bill, your share, a fee. 제가 낼게요 (I'll pay), which you know from Everyday Korean phrases, can be the whole bill or your part of it. 각자 내요 is "let's each pay our own", and 나눠서 내요 comes in the next step.
- **계산하다** is settling the bill at the counter, whoever pays for whom."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-paying-2a> ,
                         <#q-paying-2b> .

<#q-paying-2a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-28T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "커피는 제가 살게요"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "The coffee's on me"@en ,
                    "Kaffet bjuder jag på"@sv ,
                    "Den Kaffee übernehme ich"@de ,
                    "El café lo pago yo"@es ,
                    "Le café, c'est moi qui l'offre"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said in polite 해요체 to a friend or acquaintance who has just paid for the meal: a common way to return a treat at once. 는 sets the coffee against the meal (the meal was you, the coffee is me), and -(으)ㄹ게요 says what the speaker will do. The usual reply is 좋아요, 잘 마실게요."@en ,
                        "Sägs i artig 해요체 till en vän eller bekant som just har betalat maten: ett vanligt sätt att genast bjuda tillbaka. 는 ställer kaffet mot maten (maten var din, kaffet är mitt), och -(으)ㄹ게요 säger vad den som talar ska göra. Det vanliga svaret är 좋아요, 잘 마실게요."@sv ,
                        "Sagt man im höflichen 해요체 zu Freunden oder Bekannten, die gerade das Essen bezahlt haben: eine übliche Art, sich gleich zu revanchieren. 는 stellt den Kaffee dem Essen gegenüber (das Essen hast du bezahlt, den Kaffee zahle ich), und -(으)ㄹ게요 sagt, was der Sprechende tun wird. Die übliche Antwort ist 좋아요, 잘 마실게요."@de ,
                        "Se dice en el estilo cortés 해요체 a un amigo o conocido que acaba de pagar la comida: una forma habitual de devolver la invitación enseguida. 는 contrapone el café a la comida (la comida, tú; el café, yo), y -(으)ㄹ게요 dice lo que hará quien habla. La respuesta habitual es 좋아요, 잘 마실게요."@es ,
                        "Se dit au style poli 해요체 à un ami ou une connaissance qui vient de payer le repas : une façon courante de rendre tout de suite l'invitation. 는 oppose le café au repas (le repas, c'était toi ; le café, c'est moi), et -(으)ㄹ게요 dit ce que fera celui qui parle. La réponse habituelle est 좋아요, 잘 마실게요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-paying-2a-d1> ,
                          <#q-paying-2a-d2> ,
                          <#q-paying-2a-d3> .

<#q-paying-2a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "The meal's on me"@en ,
                              "Maten bjuder jag på"@sv ,
                              "Das Essen übernehme ich"@de ,
                              "La comida la pago yo"@es ,
                              "Le repas, c'est moi qui l'offre"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 밥은 제가 살게요; 커피 is coffee."@en ,
                              "Det vore 밥은 제가 살게요; 커피 är kaffe."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 밥은 제가 살게요; 커피 ist Kaffee."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 밥은 제가 살게요; 커피 es café."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 밥은 제가 살게요 ; 커피 veut dire café."@fr .

