<#ch-delivery-3>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-delivery> ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Leave it at the door

*Another way the evening could go: Alex orders the same dinner on a delivery app instead. Under the order there is a box for requests, 요청 사항, and a box to tick for no disposable spoons and chopsticks. Alex types:*

**요청 사항:** 문 앞에 두고 가 주세요.\\
*Request: Please leave it at the door.*

*Half an hour later, the doorbell rings.*

**배달 기사:** 배달 왔습니다! 문 앞에 두고 갈게요.\\
*Your delivery's here! I'll leave it at the door.*

**알렉스:** 네, 감사합니다!\\
*Great, thank you!*

On the phone, Alex could have turned down the spoons and chopsticks at the end of the order instead of ticking the box:

**알렉스:** 수저는 안 주셔도 돼요.\\
*No need for spoons and chopsticks.*

**직원:** 네, 알겠습니다.\\
*Certainly.*

---

**문 앞에 두고 가 주세요**: "Please leave it at the door." 문 is a door and 앞 the front of it; 두다 is to put down or leave, so 두고 가다 is "leave it and go".

**수저는 안 주셔도 돼요**: "No need for spoons and chopsticks." 수저 is a spoon and chopsticks together. 안 -아/어도 돼요 means "it's fine not to", and 주셔도 is 주다 with -시-, honoring the staff who would give them.

**배달 왔습니다**: "Your delivery's here." It is the set line of delivery riders, in 합쇼체: literally "the delivery has come". 배달 기사 is the delivery rider.

**Culture note:** Delivery is everywhere in Korea, and most of it is ordered through apps such as 배달의민족, 쿠팡이츠 and 요기요, but a neighborhood 중국집 still takes orders by phone. 짜장면 on a rainy day is a well-known habit, and so are 파전 and 막걸리. Many places have a minimum order and add a delivery fee, 배달비. Since the COVID-19 pandemic, leaving the food at the door without meeting, 비대면, has become the usual way: the rider rings and goes. Some old-style 중국집 still deliver in real bowls and come back for them, so you put the empty bowls outside the door afterwards."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-delivery-3a> ,
                         <#q-delivery-3b> .

<#q-delivery-3a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-28T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "문 앞에 두고 가 주세요"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Please leave it at the door"@en ,
                    "Lämna det utanför dörren, tack"@sv ,
                    "Bitte stellen Sie es vor die Tür"@de ,
                    "Déjelo en la puerta, por favor"@es ,
                    "Laissez-le devant la porte, s'il vous plaît"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said by a customer to a delivery rider, or typed in the request box of a delivery app, in polite 해요체. Literally \"put it in front of the door and go\": 두다 is to put down or leave. The rider answers 네, 알겠습니다, or simply rings, leaves the order outside and goes."@en ,
                        "Sägs av en kund till ett matbud, eller skrivs i rutan för önskemål i en matleveransapp, i artig 해요체. Ordagrant ”lägg det framför dörren och gå”: 두다 är att ställa ifrån sig eller lämna. Budet svarar 네, 알겠습니다, eller ringer bara på, lämnar beställningen utanför och går."@sv ,
                        "Sagt ein Kunde zu einem Lieferfahrer, oder in das Feld für Wünsche einer Liefer-App geschrieben, im höflichen 해요체. Wörtlich „stellen Sie es vor die Tür und gehen Sie“: 두다 heißt abstellen oder lassen. Der Fahrer antwortet 네, 알겠습니다, oder klingelt einfach, stellt die Bestellung ab und geht."@de ,
                        "Lo dice un cliente a un repartidor, o se escribe en la casilla de peticiones de una aplicación de comida a domicilio, en el estilo cortés 해요체. Literalmente «déjelo delante de la puerta y váyase»: 두다 es dejar o poner. El repartidor responde 네, 알겠습니다, o simplemente llama al timbre, deja el pedido fuera y se va."@es ,
                        "Dit par un client à un livreur, ou écrit dans la case des demandes d'une application de livraison, au style poli 해요체. Littéralement « posez-le devant la porte et partez » : 두다 veut dire poser ou laisser. Le livreur répond 네, 알겠습니다, ou bien sonne, laisse la commande devant la porte et repart."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-delivery-3a-d1> ,
                          <#q-delivery-3a-d2> ,
                          <#q-delivery-3a-d3> .

<#q-delivery-3a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Please knock instead of ringing"@en ,
                              "Knacka i stället för att ringa på, tack"@sv ,
                              "Bitte klopfen Sie, statt zu klingeln"@de ,
                              "Toque a la puerta en vez del timbre, por favor"@es ,
                              "Frappez au lieu de sonner, s'il vous plaît"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 벨 누르지 말고 노크해 주세요; 두고 가다 is to leave something and go."@en ,
                              "Det vore 벨 누르지 말고 노크해 주세요; 두고 가다 är att lämna något och gå."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 벨 누르지 말고 노크해 주세요; 두고 가다 heißt, etwas abzustellen und zu gehen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 벨 누르지 말고 노크해 주세요; 두고 가다 es dejar algo e irse."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 벨 누르지 말고 노크해 주세요 ; 두고 가다 veut dire laisser quelque chose et partir."@fr .

