# Chapter 6: Cooking together.
<#ch-cooking>
    a solid-memo:Chapter ,
      schema:Syllabus ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <> ;
    schema:position 6 ;
    dcterms:title "Cooking together"@en ,
                  "Vi lagar mat tillsammans"@sv ,
                  "Zusammen kochen"@de ,
                  "Cocinamos juntos"@es ,
                  "On cuisine ensemble"@fr ,
                  "같이 요리해요"@ko ;
    dcterms:description "Back at Alex's flat with the shopping, Alex and Minji cook a mild 떡볶이 and agree to speak casually: suggesting 반말, then asking for things in the kitchen, tasting for seasoning and calling each other to eat in the casual style. Ends with a review of the chapter."@en ,
                        "Tillbaka hemma hos Alex med matkassarna lagar Alex och Minji en mild 떡볶이 och kommer överens om att prata vardagligt: att föreslå 반말 och sedan be om saker i köket, smaka av kryddningen och ropa på varandra att maten är klar i den vardagliga stilen. Avslutas med en repetition av kapitlet."@sv ,
                        "Mit den Einkäufen zurück in Alex' Wohnung kochen Alex und Minji ein mildes 떡볶이 und einigen sich darauf, ungezwungen miteinander zu reden: 반말 vorschlagen, dann in der Küche um Dinge bitten, abschmecken und sich im lockeren Stil zum Essen rufen. Endet mit einer Wiederholung des Kapitels."@de ,
                        "De vuelta en el piso de Alex con la compra, Alex y Minji cocinan un 떡볶이 suave y acuerdan hablarse de manera informal: proponer el 반말 y luego pedir cosas en la cocina, probar el punto de sal y llamarse a comer en el estilo informal. Termina con un repaso del capítulo."@es ,
                        "De retour chez Alex avec les courses, Alex et Minji cuisinent un 떡볶이 doux et décident de se parler de façon familière : proposer le 반말, puis demander des choses en cuisine, goûter l'assaisonnement et s'appeler à table dans le style familier. Se termine par une révision du chapitre."@fr ;
    solid-memo:reviewQuestion <#q-cooking-r01> ,
                              <#q-cooking-r02> .

<#ch-cooking-1>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-cooking> ;
    schema:position 0 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Shall we drop the formalities?

*The same Saturday afternoon. Back at Alex's small flat in 망원동, the shopping from the market is on the kitchen counter: rice cakes, fish cake and green onions for the mild 떡볶이 that Minji saved for another day when they first met.*

**민지:** 알렉스 씨, 우리 동갑인데 이제 말 놓을까요?\\
*Alex, we're the same age. Shall we speak casually with each other now?*

**알렉스:** 좋아요! … 아, 좋아!\\
*Sure! … Oh, I mean: sure!*

**민지:** 하하, 그래, 좋아. 칼 어디 있어?\\
*Ha ha, okay, great. Where's the knife?*

**알렉스:** 서랍에 있어. 아, 민지야, 간장 좀 줘.\\
*In the drawer. Oh, Minji, pass me the soy sauce.*

**민지:** 여기. 그리고 불 좀 줄여 줘. 불이 너무 세.\\
*Here. And turn the heat down a bit. It's too high.*

**알렉스:** 알았어.\\
*Okay.*

---

**우리 말 놓을까요?**: "Shall we speak casually with each other?" 말을 놓다, literally "to put down one's words", means to drop polite speech with someone. Minji still asks in 해요체, since the switch has not happened yet, and being 동갑 (the same age), as they found out at the café, makes the question natural. -인데 adds the reason: "we're the same age, so …".

**좋아요! … 아, 좋아!**: "Sure! … I mean: sure!" Once both agree, they switch at once, and Alex's answer is the switch itself. Here 반말 is 해요체 without the final 요: 좋아요 becomes 좋아, 있어요 becomes 있어, 줘요 becomes 줘. 씨 goes too: Alex now calls her 민지야, and from here on every line between them is casual, though the English glosses can't show it.

**칼 어디 있어?**: "Where's the knife?" The answer **서랍에 있어** means "it's in the drawer".

**간장 좀 줘**: "Pass me the soy sauce." 줘 is 주다 in 반말; to someone you speak politely to, it would be 간장 좀 주세요. 여기 (here) is what you say as you hand it over.

**불 좀 줄여 줘**: "Turn the heat down a bit." 불 means fire, here the heat of the stove, and 줄이다 means to reduce; 줄여 줘 asks the other person to do it. 불이 너무 세 means the heat is too high, and 알았어 (okay, got it) is the casual form of 알았어요."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-cooking-1a> ,
                         <#q-cooking-1b> .

<#q-cooking-1a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-28T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "우리 말 놓을까요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Shall we speak casually with each other?"@en ,
                    "Ska vi prata vardagligt med varandra?"@sv ,
                    "Wollen wir ungezwungen miteinander reden?"@de ,
                    "¿Nos hablamos de manera informal?"@es ,
                    "On se parle de façon familière ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Asked between two adults who have spoken politely so far, usually by the older one, or by either of two people of the same age. It is still in 해요체, since the switch to 반말 has not happened yet. 말을 놓다, literally \"to put down one's words\", means to drop polite speech. The usual reply is 좋아요, or 좋아! in 반말 straight away."@en ,
                        "Frågas mellan två vuxna som hittills har pratat artigt med varandra, oftast av den äldre, eller av vem som helst av två som är lika gamla. Frågan ställs fortfarande i 해요체, eftersom bytet till 반말 inte har skett än. 말을 놓다, ordagrant ”lägga ner sina ord”, betyder att sluta tala artigt. Det vanliga svaret är 좋아요, eller direkt på 반말: 좋아!"@sv ,
                        "Gefragt zwischen zwei Erwachsenen, die bisher höflich miteinander gesprochen haben, meist vom Älteren oder von einem von zwei Gleichaltrigen. Die Frage steht noch im 해요체, weil der Wechsel zum 반말 noch nicht stattgefunden hat. 말을 놓다, wörtlich „seine Worte ablegen“, heißt, die höfliche Sprache aufzugeben. Die übliche Antwort ist 좋아요 oder gleich im 반말: 좋아!"@de ,
                        "Entre dos adultos que hasta ahora se han hablado con cortesía, lo pregunta normalmente el mayor, o cualquiera de los dos si tienen la misma edad. Sigue en 해요체, porque el cambio al 반말 aún no se ha hecho. 말을 놓다, literalmente «dejar las palabras», significa dejar de hablar con cortesía. La respuesta habitual es 좋아요, o directamente en 반말: 좋아!"@es ,
                        "Se demande entre deux adultes qui se parlaient poliment jusque-là, d'ordinaire par le plus âgé, ou par l'un ou l'autre s'ils ont le même âge. La question reste au 해요체, puisque le passage au 반말 n'a pas encore eu lieu. 말을 놓다, littéralement « poser ses paroles », veut dire abandonner le langage poli. La réponse habituelle est 좋아요, ou tout de suite en 반말 : 좋아 !"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-cooking-1a-d1> ,
                          <#q-cooking-1a-d2> ,
                          <#q-cooking-1a-d3> .

<#q-cooking-1a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Shall we speak more politely with each other?"@en ,
                              "Ska vi prata artigare med varandra?"@sv ,
                              "Wollen wir höflicher miteinander reden?"@de ,
                              "¿Nos hablamos de manera más formal?"@es ,
                              "On se parle de façon plus polie ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 우리 존댓말 쓸까요?; 말을 놓다 means dropping polite speech, not taking it up."@en ,
                              "Det vore 우리 존댓말 쓸까요?; 말을 놓다 betyder att sluta tala artigt, inte att börja."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 우리 존댓말 쓸까요?; 말을 놓다 heißt, die höfliche Sprache aufzugeben, nicht, sie anzunehmen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 우리 존댓말 쓸까요?; 말을 놓다 significa dejar de hablar con cortesía, no empezar."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 우리 존댓말 쓸까요? ; 말을 놓다 veut dire abandonner le langage poli, pas l'adopter."@fr .

<#q-cooking-1a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Shall we speak English with each other?"@en ,
                              "Ska vi prata engelska med varandra?"@sv ,
                              "Wollen wir Englisch miteinander reden?"@de ,
                              "¿Nos hablamos en inglés?"@es ,
                              "On se parle en anglais ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 우리 영어로 말할까요?; 말을 놓다 is about the speech level, not the language."@en ,
                              "Det vore 우리 영어로 말할까요?; 말을 놓다 handlar om artighetsnivån, inte om språket."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 우리 영어로 말할까요?; 말을 놓다 betrifft die Sprechstufe, nicht die Sprache."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 우리 영어로 말할까요?; 말을 놓다 se refiere al nivel de cortesía, no al idioma."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 우리 영어로 말할까요? ; 말을 놓다 porte sur le niveau de politesse, pas sur la langue."@fr .

<#q-cooking-1a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Shall we put it down here?"@en ,
                              "Ska vi ställa ner det här?"@sv ,
                              "Sollen wir es hier abstellen?"@de ,
                              "¿Lo dejamos aquí?"@es ,
                              "On le pose ici ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "A literal reading: 놓다 alone means to put down, as in 여기 놓을까요?, but 말을 놓다 is about how you speak to each other."@en ,
                              "En ordagrann läsning: 놓다 ensamt betyder att ställa eller lägga ner, som i 여기 놓을까요?, men 말을 놓다 handlar om hur man talar till varandra."@sv ,
                              "Eine wörtliche Lesart: 놓다 allein heißt abstellen oder hinlegen, wie in 여기 놓을까요?, aber 말을 놓다 betrifft, wie man miteinander spricht."@de ,
                              "Una lectura literal: 놓다 solo significa dejar o poner, como en 여기 놓을까요?, pero 말을 놓다 se refiere a cómo se hablan."@es ,
                              "Une lecture littérale : 놓다 seul veut dire poser, comme dans 여기 놓을까요?, mais 말을 놓다 porte sur la façon de se parler."@fr .

<#q-cooking-1b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-28T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "간장 좀 줘"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Pass me the soy sauce (to a close friend)"@en ,
                    "Skicka sojasåsen (till en nära vän)"@sv ,
                    "Gib mir mal die Sojasoße (unter engen Freunden)"@de ,
                    "Pásame la salsa de soja (a un amigo cercano)"@es ,
                    "Passe-moi la sauce soja (à un ami proche)"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said in 반말 to a close friend, a younger sibling or a child, or between adults who have agreed to speak casually. 줘 is 주다 in 반말, and 좀 softens the request; to someone you speak politely to, you say 간장 좀 주세요. The usual reply is 여기 (here) as it is handed over."@en ,
                        "Sägs på 반말 till en nära vän, ett yngre syskon eller ett barn, eller mellan vuxna som har kommit överens om att prata vardagligt. 줘 är 주다 på 반말, och 좀 mjukar upp begäran; till någon man talar artigt med säger man 간장 좀 주세요. Det vanliga svaret är 여기 (här) när man räcker över den."@sv ,
                        "Gesagt im 반말 zu engen Freunden, jüngeren Geschwistern oder Kindern oder unter Erwachsenen, die vereinbart haben, ungezwungen zu reden. 줘 ist 주다 im 반말, und 좀 macht die Bitte weicher; zu jemandem, mit dem man höflich spricht, sagt man 간장 좀 주세요. Die übliche Antwort ist 여기 (hier) beim Hinüberreichen."@de ,
                        "Se dice en 반말 a un amigo cercano, a un hermano menor o a un niño, o entre adultos que han acordado hablarse de manera informal. 줘 es 주다 en 반말, y 좀 suaviza la petición; a alguien a quien se habla con cortesía se le dice 간장 좀 주세요. La respuesta habitual es 여기 (aquí) al pasarla."@es ,
                        "Se dit en 반말 à un ami proche, à un frère ou une sœur plus jeune ou à un enfant, ou entre adultes qui ont convenu de se parler de façon familière. 줘 est 주다 en 반말, et 좀 adoucit la demande ; à quelqu'un à qui l'on parle poliment, on dit 간장 좀 주세요. La réponse habituelle est 여기 (tiens) en la tendant."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-cooking-1b-d1> ,
                          <#q-cooking-1b-d2> ,
                          <#q-cooking-1b-d3> .

