<#ch-cooking-2>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-cooking> ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## From 해요체 to 반말

Most of 반말 is 해요체 with the final 요 left off. A few words change too:

- **Drop 요**: 먹어요 becomes 먹어, 줘요 becomes 줘, 있어요 becomes 있어, 맛있어요 becomes 맛있어.
- **이에요/예요 become 이야/야**: 이야 after a consonant and 야 after a vowel, so 이거 진짜 맛있는 떡볶이야 (this is really good tteokbokki).
- **Yes and no**: 네 becomes 응, and 아니요 becomes 아니.
- **I and me**: 저 becomes 나, 제가 becomes 내가, 저도 becomes 나도.
- **Names**: 씨 is dropped, and a name you call out takes 아 after a consonant and 야 after a vowel: 수진아, 민지야. With a foreign name like 알렉스, many people just say the name.

**알렉스:** 민지야, 간 좀 봐 줘.\\
*Minji, taste it for seasoning, would you?*

**민지:** 음, 좀 싱거워. 간장 조금만 더 넣어.\\
*Hmm, it's a bit bland. Add just a little more soy sauce.*

**알렉스:** 이 정도?\\
*About this much?*

**민지:** 응, 딱 좋아. 됐다! 이제 먹자.\\
*Yes, just right. Done! Let's eat now.*

---

**Suggesting in 반말.** The endings -(으)ㄹ까요? and -(으)ㄹ래요?, which you know from choosing dinner, lose their 요 too, and one is new:

- **-자** means "let's": 먹자, 가자, 하자. Between friends who speak politely, the same idea is 먹어요 or 먹을까요?
- **-(으)ㄹ까?** means "shall we?" or "shall I?": 먹을까?, 갈까?
- **-(으)ㄹ래?** means "do you want to?": 먹을래?, 갈래?

**Asking in 반말.** -아/어 주세요 becomes -아/어 줘: 봐 줘 (have a look for me), 줄여 줘 (turn it down for me), 넣어 줘 (put it in for me). A plain command, like Minji's 넣어 (put it in), is fine between close friends.

**간 좀 봐 줘**: "Taste it for seasoning, would you?" 간 is the seasoning, mostly how salty a dish is, and 간을 보다 means to taste it to check. Too little is 싱거워 (bland), too much is 짜 (salty), and 딱 좋아 is just right.

**이제 먹자**: "Let's eat now." 이제 means now, after waiting. 됐다! is an exclamation: "done!" or "that's it!"."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-cooking-2a> ,
                         <#q-cooking-2b> .

<#q-cooking-2a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-28T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "간 좀 봐 줘"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Taste it for seasoning, would you? (to a close friend)"@en ,
                    "Smaka av kryddningen, är du snäll (till en nära vän)"@sv ,
                    "Schmeck mal ab (unter engen Freunden)"@de ,
                    "Prueba a ver qué tal de sal (a un amigo cercano)"@es ,
                    "Goûte voir si c'est assez salé (à un ami proche)"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said in 반말 while cooking, to a close friend or family member, asking them to taste the dish and say whether it needs more salt or soy sauce. 간 is the seasoning, mostly how salty a dish is, and 간을 보다 means to taste to check it; 봐 줘 is the 반말 of 봐 주세요. The usual reply is 응, 좀 싱거워 (a bit bland), 좀 짜 (a bit salty) or 딱 좋아 (just right)."@en ,
                        "Sägs på 반말 när man lagar mat, till en nära vän eller någon i familjen, för att be dem smaka på rätten och säga om den behöver mer salt eller sojasås. 간 är kryddningen, främst hur salt en rätt är, och 간을 보다 betyder att smaka av; 봐 줘 är 반말 för 봐 주세요. Det vanliga svaret är 응, 좀 싱거워 (lite smaklös), 좀 짜 (lite salt) eller 딱 좋아 (precis lagom)."@sv ,
                        "Gesagt im 반말 beim Kochen, zu engen Freunden oder Familienmitgliedern, mit der Bitte, das Gericht zu kosten und zu sagen, ob es mehr Salz oder Sojasoße braucht. 간 ist die Würze, vor allem wie salzig ein Gericht ist, und 간을 보다 heißt abschmecken; 봐 줘 ist das 반말 von 봐 주세요. Die übliche Antwort ist 응, 좀 싱거워 (etwas fad), 좀 짜 (etwas salzig) oder 딱 좋아 (genau richtig)."@de ,
                        "Se dice en 반말 al cocinar, a un amigo cercano o a alguien de la familia, para pedirle que pruebe el plato y diga si le falta sal o salsa de soja. 간 es el punto de sal de un plato, y 간을 보다 significa probarlo para comprobarlo; 봐 줘 es el 반말 de 봐 주세요. La respuesta habitual es 응, 좀 싱거워 (un poco soso), 좀 짜 (un poco salado) o 딱 좋아 (perfecto)."@es ,
                        "Se dit en 반말 en cuisinant, à un ami proche ou à quelqu'un de la famille, pour lui demander de goûter le plat et de dire s'il manque de sel ou de sauce soja. 간 est l'assaisonnement, surtout le degré de sel d'un plat, et 간을 보다 veut dire goûter pour le vérifier ; 봐 줘 est le 반말 de 봐 주세요. La réponse habituelle est 응, 좀 싱거워 (un peu fade), 좀 짜 (un peu salé) ou 딱 좋아 (parfait)."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-cooking-2a-d1> ,
                          <#q-cooking-2a-d2> ,
                          <#q-cooking-2a-d3> .

<#q-cooking-2a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Taste it for seasoning, would you? (to someone older)"@en ,
                              "Kan du smaka av kryddningen? (till någon äldre)"@sv ,
                              "Schmecken Sie bitte mal ab (zu jemand Älterem)"@de ,
                              "Pruebe a ver qué tal de sal (a alguien mayor)"@es ,
                              "Goûtez voir si c'est assez salé (à quelqu'un de plus âgé)"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 간 좀 봐 주세요; 봐 줘 without 요 is 반말, for close friends and family."@en ,
                              "Det vore 간 좀 봐 주세요; 봐 줘 utan 요 är 반말, för nära vänner och familj."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 간 좀 봐 주세요; 봐 줘 ohne 요 ist 반말, für enge Freunde und die Familie."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 간 좀 봐 주세요; 봐 줘 sin 요 es 반말, para amigos cercanos y la familia."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 간 좀 봐 주세요 ; 봐 줘 sans 요 est du 반말, pour les amis proches et la famille."@fr .

<#q-cooking-2a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Check whether it's spicy, would you? (to a close friend)"@en ,
                              "Kolla om det är starkt, är du snäll (till en nära vän)"@sv ,
                              "Probier mal, ob es scharf ist (unter engen Freunden)"@de ,
                              "Prueba a ver si pica (a un amigo cercano)"@es ,
                              "Goûte voir si c'est piquant (à un ami proche)"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 매운지 맛 좀 봐 줘; 간 is about salt and seasoning, not spice."@en ,
                              "Det vore 매운지 맛 좀 봐 줘; 간 handlar om salt och kryddning, inte om hetta."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 매운지 맛 좀 봐 줘; 간 betrifft Salz und Würze, nicht die Schärfe."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 매운지 맛 좀 봐 줘; 간 se refiere a la sal, no al picante."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 매운지 맛 좀 봐 줘 ; 간 porte sur le sel et l'assaisonnement, pas sur le piquant."@fr .

<#q-cooking-2a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Keep an eye on the pot, would you? (to a close friend)"@en ,
                              "Håll ett öga på grytan, är du snäll (till en nära vän)"@sv ,
                              "Pass mal auf den Topf auf (unter engen Freunden)"@de ,
                              "Vigila la olla (a un amigo cercano)"@es ,
                              "Surveille la casserole (à un ami proche)"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 냄비 좀 봐 줘; 봐 주다 can mean to look after, but 간을 보다 is to taste for seasoning."@en ,
                              "Det vore 냄비 좀 봐 줘; 봐 주다 kan betyda att hålla ett öga på, men 간을 보다 är att smaka av."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 냄비 좀 봐 줘; 봐 주다 kann aufpassen heißen, aber 간을 보다 ist abschmecken."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 냄비 좀 봐 줘; 봐 주다 puede significar vigilar, pero 간을 보다 es probar el punto de sal."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 냄비 좀 봐 줘 ; 봐 주다 peut vouloir dire surveiller, mais 간을 보다 veut dire goûter l'assaisonnement."@fr .

<#q-cooking-2b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-28T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "이제 먹자"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Let's eat now (to a close friend)"@en ,
                    "Nu äter vi (till en nära vän)"@sv ,
                    "Lass uns jetzt essen (unter engen Freunden)"@de ,
                    "Vamos a comer ya (a un amigo cercano)"@es ,
                    "Maintenant, on mange (à un ami proche)"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said in 반말 to close friends or family when the food is ready. -자 means \"let's\" and is only used in 반말; between people who speak politely, the same idea is 이제 먹어요 or 이제 먹을까요? 이제 means now, after waiting. The usual reply is 응, 먹자! and then 잘 먹겠습니다, which anyone says before eating."@en ,
                        "Sägs på 반말 till nära vänner eller familj när maten är klar. -자 betyder ”låt oss” och används bara på 반말; mellan människor som talar artigt blir samma sak 이제 먹어요 eller 이제 먹을까요? 이제 betyder nu, efter en väntan. Det vanliga svaret är 응, 먹자! och sedan 잘 먹겠습니다, som alla säger innan de äter."@sv ,
                        "Gesagt im 반말 zu engen Freunden oder zur Familie, wenn das Essen fertig ist. -자 heißt „lass uns“ und kommt nur im 반말 vor; unter Leuten, die höflich miteinander sprechen, heißt dasselbe 이제 먹어요 oder 이제 먹을까요? 이제 heißt jetzt, nach dem Warten. Die übliche Antwort ist 응, 먹자! und dann 잘 먹겠습니다, was jeder vor dem Essen sagt."@de ,
                        "Se dice en 반말 a amigos cercanos o a la familia cuando la comida está lista. -자 significa «vamos a» y solo se usa en 반말; entre personas que se hablan con cortesía, lo mismo es 이제 먹어요 o 이제 먹을까요? 이제 significa ahora, tras la espera. La respuesta habitual es 응, 먹자! y luego 잘 먹겠습니다, que todo el mundo dice antes de comer."@es ,
                        "Se dit en 반말 à des amis proches ou à la famille quand le repas est prêt. -자 veut dire « allons » et ne s'emploie qu'en 반말 ; entre personnes qui se parlent poliment, on dit 이제 먹어요 ou 이제 먹을까요? 이제 veut dire maintenant, après l'attente. La réponse habituelle est 응, 먹자 ! puis 잘 먹겠습니다, que tout le monde dit avant de manger."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-cooking-2b-d1> ,
                          <#q-cooking-2b-d2> ,
                          <#q-cooking-2b-d3> .

<#q-cooking-2b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Shall we eat now? (to an acquaintance)"@en ,
                              "Ska vi äta nu? (till en bekant)"@sv ,
                              "Wollen wir jetzt essen? (zu einem Bekannten)"@de ,
                              "¿Comemos ahora? (a un conocido)"@es ,
                              "On mange maintenant ? (à une connaissance)"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 이제 먹을까요?; -자 is 반말, only for close friends and family."@en ,
                              "Det vore 이제 먹을까요?; -자 är 반말, bara för nära vänner och familj."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 이제 먹을까요?; -자 ist 반말, nur für enge Freunde und die Familie."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 이제 먹을까요?; -자 es 반말, solo para amigos cercanos y la familia."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 이제 먹을까요? ; -자 est du 반말, réservé aux amis proches et à la famille."@fr .

<#q-cooking-2b-d2>
