<#ch-family-3>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-family> ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Thank you for having me

*Another way it goes: dinner is over, and the table is being cleared. Alex gets up to help.*

**알렉스:** 어머님, 설거지는 제가 할게요.\\
*I'll do the dishes.*

**어머니:** 아니에요, 손님인데 그냥 앉아 있어요.\\
*Oh no, you're our guest. Just stay where you are.*

**민지:** 엄마, 그럼 내가 할게.\\
*Mom, I'll do them, then.*

*Later, at the door, shoes back on:*

**알렉스:** 오늘 초대해 주셔서 감사합니다. 정말 잘 먹었습니다.\\
*Thank you for inviting me today. It was a wonderful meal.*

**어머니:** 와 줘서 고마워요. 또 놀러 와요.\\
*Thank you for coming. Come and visit again.*

**아버지:** 조심히 가요.\\
*Get home safely.*

**알렉스:** 네, 안녕히 계세요.\\
*I will. Goodbye.*

---

**설거지는 제가 할게요**: "I'll do the dishes." 설거지 is washing up. Offering is polite, and the host turning it down, as here, is just as expected.

**초대해 주셔서 감사합니다**: "Thank you for inviting me." -아/어 주셔서 감사합니다 thanks someone for doing something for you, and -시- in 주셔서 honors the hosts. It is a set line in 합쇼체, said on leaving or on arriving, here with 잘 먹었습니다, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases.

**또 놀러 와요**: "Come and visit again." 놀러 오다, literally "come to play", is the everyday way to say come over. Minji's mother says it in plain 해요체, like 와 줘서 고마워요 (thank you for coming). The father's 조심히 가요 is 조심히 가세요, from Everyday Korean phrases, without -시-, as an older person may say it to someone young.

**안녕히 계세요**, from Basic Korean, is said by the one who leaves to those who stay; those who stay say 안녕히 가세요.

**Culture note:** When you visit a family at home, bring something: a box of fruit such as pears or apples, juice or a gift set is the usual choice, handed over with both hands. Shoes come off at the door. At the table, wait until the eldest has picked up the spoon or chopsticks before you start, and try not to leave the table before the elders have finished. Praise the food, and offer to help afterward; the host will usually say no, and that is fine. A friend's parents are 어머님 and 아버님 to you."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-family-3a> ,
                         <#q-family-3b> .

<#q-family-3a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-28T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "초대해 주셔서 감사합니다"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Thank you for inviting me"@en ,
                    "Tack för inbjudan"@sv ,
                    "Vielen Dank für die Einladung"@de ,
                    "Gracias por invitarme"@es ,
                    "Merci pour l'invitation"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said by a guest to the hosts, on leaving or on arriving, in formal 합쇼체, the usual level for set thanks like this; -시- in 주셔서 honors the hosts. -아/어 주셔서 감사합니다 thanks someone for doing something for you. The hosts answer 와 줘서 고마워요 or 또 놀러 와요."@en ,
                        "Sägs av en gäst till värdarna, när man går eller när man kommer, i formell 합쇼체, den vanliga nivån för fasta tackfraser som den här; -시- i 주셔서 hedrar värdarna. -아/어 주셔서 감사합니다 tackar någon för att ha gjort något för en. Värdarna svarar 와 줘서 고마워요 eller 또 놀러 와요."@sv ,
                        "Sagt ein Gast zu den Gastgebern, beim Gehen oder beim Ankommen, im förmlichen 합쇼체, der üblichen Stufe für feste Dankesformeln wie diese; -시- in 주셔서 ehrt die Gastgeber. -아/어 주셔서 감사합니다 dankt jemandem dafür, dass er etwas für einen getan hat. Die Gastgeber antworten 와 줘서 고마워요 oder 또 놀러 와요."@de ,
                        "Lo dice un invitado a los anfitriones, al irse o al llegar, en el estilo formal 합쇼체, el nivel habitual para agradecimientos fijos como este; -시- en 주셔서 honra a los anfitriones. -아/어 주셔서 감사합니다 agradece a alguien que haya hecho algo por uno. Los anfitriones responden 와 줘서 고마워요 o 또 놀러 와요."@es ,
                        "Dit par un invité à ses hôtes, en partant ou en arrivant, au style formel 합쇼체, le niveau habituel des remerciements tout faits comme celui-ci ; -시- dans 주셔서 honore les hôtes. -아/어 주셔서 감사합니다 remercie quelqu'un d'avoir fait quelque chose pour soi. Les hôtes répondent 와 줘서 고마워요 ou 또 놀러 와요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-family-3a-d1> ,
                          <#q-family-3a-d2> ,
                          <#q-family-3a-d3> .

