                              "¡Por nuestra empresa! (un brindis)"@es ,
                              "À notre entreprise ! (un toast)"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 우리 회사를 위하여!; 팀 is the team, 회사 the company."@en ,
                              "Det vore 우리 회사를 위하여!; 팀 är teamet, 회사 företaget."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 우리 회사를 위하여!; 팀 ist das Team, 회사 die Firma."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 우리 회사를 위하여!; 팀 es el equipo, 회사 la empresa."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 우리 회사를 위하여! ; 팀 est l'équipe, 회사 l'entreprise."@fr .

<#q-hoesik-r02-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It's all thanks to our team! (in a speech)"@en ,
                              "Det är vårt teams förtjänst! (i ett tal)"@sv ,
                              "Das verdanken wir unserem Team! (in einer Rede)"@de ,
                              "¡Todo es gracias a nuestro equipo! (en un discurso)"@es ,
                              "C'est grâce à notre équipe ! (dans un discours)"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 다 우리 팀 덕분입니다; 위하여 means \"for the sake of\" and calls the toast."@en ,
                              "Det vore 다 우리 팀 덕분입니다; 위하여 betyder ”för … skull” och utbringar skålen."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 다 우리 팀 덕분입니다; 위하여 heißt „um … willen“ und bringt den Trinkspruch aus."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 다 우리 팀 덕분입니다; 위하여 significa «por el bien de» y da paso al brindis."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 다 우리 팀 덕분입니다 ; 위하여 veut dire « pour le bien de » et lance le toast."@fr .

# Chapter 9: Our regular place.
<#ch-regular>
    a solid-memo:Chapter ,
      schema:Syllabus ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <> ;
    schema:position 9 ;
    dcterms:title "Our regular place"@en ,
                  "Vårt stamställe"@sv ,
                  "Unser Stammlokal"@de ,
                  "Nuestro sitio de siempre"@es ,
                  "Notre restaurant habituel"@fr ,
                  "단골집에서"@ko ;
    dcterms:description "Months later, Alex and Minji are regulars at the stew restaurant where they shared their first meal: polite to the owner, casual to each other, honorific to a senior on the phone, and finally the casual 밥 먹었어? Ends with a review of the chapter."@en ,
                        "Månader senare är Alex och Minji stamgäster på grytrestaurangen där de åt sin första måltid tillsammans: artiga mot ägaren, vardagliga mot varandra, hedrande mot en överordnad i telefon och till sist det vardagliga 밥 먹었어? Avslutas med en repetition av kapitlet."@sv ,
                        "Monate später sind Alex und Minji Stammgäste in dem Eintopfrestaurant, in dem sie zum ersten Mal zusammen gegessen haben: höflich zum Inhaber, ungezwungen zueinander, ehrerbietig zur Teamleitung am Telefon und am Ende das lockere 밥 먹었어? Endet mit einer Wiederholung des Kapitels."@de ,
                        "Meses después, el restaurante de guisos de la primera comida de Alex y Minji es ya su sitio de siempre: cortesía con el dueño, tuteo entre amigos, honoríficos con un superior al teléfono y, al final, el informal 밥 먹었어? Termina con un repaso del capítulo."@es ,
                        "Des mois plus tard, le restaurant de ragoûts du premier repas d'Alex et de Minji est devenu leur cantine : politesse avec le patron, familiarité entre amis, déférence envers un supérieur au téléphone, et pour finir le familier 밥 먹었어? Se termine par une révision du chapitre."@fr ;
    solid-memo:reviewQuestion <#q-regular-r01> ,
                              <#q-regular-r02> .

<#ch-regular-1>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-regular> ;
    schema:position 0 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## The usual

*Months later, a warm Friday evening in May. The small 찌개 restaurant near Hongik University station, where Alex and Minji shared their first meal, has become their regular place. The owner looks up as they come in.*

**사장님:** 어, 왔어요? 늘 앉던 자리 비어 있어요.\\
*Oh, there you are! Your usual table is free.*

**알렉스:** 감사합니다. 사장님, 늘 먹던 걸로 주세요.\\
*Thanks. The usual, please.*

**사장님:** 김치찌개 2인분이요? 알겠어요.\\
*Kimchi stew for two? Coming up.*

**알렉스:** 민지야, 뭐 더 시킬래?\\
*Minji, do you want to order anything else?*

**민지:** 아니, 충분해.\\
*No, that's plenty.*

**사장님:** 이건 서비스예요. 맛있게 드세요.\\
*This one's on the house. Enjoy.*

**알렉스:** 와, 계란말이! 감사합니다. 잘 먹겠습니다.\\
*Oh, rolled omelette! Thank you. I'll enjoy this!*

---

**늘 먹던 걸로 주세요**: "The usual, please." 늘 means always, and -던 on a verb recalls something that used to happen in the past; with 늘, 늘 먹던 거 is "what we always have", and the owner's 늘 앉던 자리 is "the seat you always sit at". 걸로 is short for 것으로, with the (으)로 for choosing from the café. The owner might confirm with -시-: 늘 드시던 걸로요?

**어, 왔어요?**: "Oh, there you are!" 어서 오세요, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases, welcomes anyone who walks in; 왔어요?, literally "you've come?", greets people the owner knows. It is warm 해요체 without -시-, as owners often speak to regulars.

**뭐 더 시킬래?**: "Do you want to order anything else?" 시키다 is the everyday word for ordering food, and 주문하다 the neutral one. 시킬래? is -(으)ㄹ래요?, met when choosing dinner, without 요, so it is 반말. Minji's 아니, 충분해 means "no, that's plenty".

**이건 서비스예요**: "This one's on the house." 서비스 comes from English "service", but in a Korean restaurant it means something given free, here a 계란말이 (rolled omelette). 잘 먹겠습니다, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases, is the thank-you before eating.

**Speech level:** in a few seconds Alex speaks politely to the owner (해요체, with the set 합쇼체 thanks 감사합니다 and 잘 먹겠습니다), 반말 to Minji, and politely again to the owner. The level follows the person you speak to, line by line."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-regular-1a> ,
                         <#q-regular-1b> .

<#q-regular-1a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-28T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "늘 먹던 걸로 주세요"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "The usual, please"@en ,
                    "Det vanliga, tack"@sv ,
                    "Das Übliche, bitte"@de ,
                    "Lo de siempre, por favor"@es ,
                    "Comme d'habitude, s'il vous plaît"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said by a regular customer to the owner or staff of a restaurant who know them, in polite 해요체. 늘 means always, and -던 recalls something that used to happen, so 늘 먹던 거 is \"what I always have\"; 걸로 is 것으로, with (으)로 for choosing. The staff answer 네, 늘 드시던 걸로요 or 알겠어요."@en ,
                        "Sägs av en stamgäst till ägaren eller personalen på en restaurang som känner igen en, i artig 해요체. 늘 betyder alltid, och -던 syftar tillbaka på något man brukade göra, så 늘 먹던 거 är ”det jag alltid tar”; 걸로 är 것으로, med (으)로 för det man väljer. Personalen svarar 네, 늘 드시던 걸로요 eller 알겠어요."@sv ,
                        "Sagt ein Stammgast zum Inhaber oder Personal eines Restaurants, das ihn kennt, im höflichen 해요체. 늘 heißt immer, und -던 verweist auf etwas, das man früher zu tun pflegte, also ist 늘 먹던 거 „das, was ich immer nehme“; 걸로 ist 것으로, mit (으)로 für die Wahl. Das Personal antwortet 네, 늘 드시던 걸로요 oder 알겠어요."@de ,
                        "Lo dice un cliente habitual al dueño o al personal de un restaurante que lo conoce, en el estilo cortés 해요체. 늘 significa siempre, y -던 remite a algo que se solía hacer, así que 늘 먹던 거 es «lo que tomo siempre»; 걸로 es 것으로, con (으)로 para lo que se elige. El personal responde 네, 늘 드시던 걸로요 o 알겠어요."@es ,
                        "Dit par un habitué au patron ou au personnel d'un restaurant qui le connaît, au style poli 해요체. 늘 veut dire toujours, et -던 renvoie à ce qu'on avait l'habitude de faire, donc 늘 먹던 거 est « ce que je prends toujours » ; 걸로 est 것으로, avec (으)로 pour ce qu'on choisit. Le personnel répond 네, 늘 드시던 걸로요 ou 알겠어요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-regular-1a-d1> ,
                          <#q-regular-1a-d2> ,
                          <#q-regular-1a-d3> .

